# Review record for executor merges (owner 2026-10-16: reviews must actually run before work is accepted).
# One line per `Merge exec/*` commit on the working branch since the delegation baseline:
#   <merge-sha-12> PASS|WAIVED|PENDING <yyyy-mm-dd> <who/why>
# PASS = the reviewer agent returned PASS on that change. WAIVED needs a reason (debug-only, docs/config,
# verified otherwise). PENDING = a review is running; scripts/delegation_check.py reports it until replaced.
# Keyed by the executor branch tip (before merge) or the merge commit. Before a merge, the
# require-review-before-merge hook needs a PASS/WAIVED line for the branch tip; after, the Stop hook
# blocks the end of a turn while any executor merge has no line.
